## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design secure, observable data pipelines across accounts, with PII masking, lineage, and governance using Lake Formation, Glue, and S3 Parquet. Focuses on practical patterns for multi-tenant data sharing and compliance.

## Key Concepts

- Lake Formation permissions and masking
- Glue Catalog and Spark-based data masking
- Parquet with schema evolution and partitioning
- Data lineage, audit via Glue Catalog/CloudTrail
- Cross-account access via RAM and trusted roles

## Code Example

```javascript
function maskPII(value, type) {
  if (type === 'ssn') return value ? value.replace(/\d{3}-\d{2}-\d{4}/g, 'XXX-XX-XXXX') : value;
  if (type === 'email') {
    const [name, domain] = (value||'').split('@');
    return (name ? name[0] + '***' : '') + '@' + (domain||'');
  }
  return value;
}
```

